    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Where I went #",
        "main_title": "Bueng Kan Walking Street",
        "author": "",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "I arrived into Bueng Kan city just before sunset. I dumped my bag at the hotel and ran down to the local night markets along the Mekong River like a giddy kid.\nBefore coming, I had heard countless good reviews about these markets, and I was not disappointed.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Amazing location along the Mekong (albeit, with some sort of large-scale construction going on between the markets and the river currently).\nI arrived during golden hour, and the entire place just shone.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The markets themselves are two or three rows of stalls. Predominately food, but plenty of options, from clothes, electronics, footwear and some knickknacks too.\nAll up, the markets would be about a kilometre long with many, MANY food options available.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "What I liked #",
        "main_title": "Bueng Kan Walking Street",
        "author": "",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "I loved this market for its variety. It was rare to see more than two types of the same food stall.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Big open area, located directly on the mighty Mekong River.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Dedicated pedestrian area. No cars or motorbikes to battle with.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Some break out areas provided to sit down and enjoy your food.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "What I ate #",
        "main_title": "Bueng Kan Walking Street",
        "author": "",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "My focus tonight was ’luuk chin’ (or small meatballs on a stick) and other satay style meats.\nI grabbed some fresh fruit to snacks on over the coming days and some sweet buns!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "No idea what I spent, but it’s a typical local market, so everything was good value",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "📷 Photos #",
        "main_title": "Bueng Kan Walking Street",
        "author": "",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "This is possibly the greatest local market in Thailand Located just behind the local hospital (with a temple in the middle of a roundabout) A more typical situated temple Where would you rather be on a Friday night? I know these are tasty, but they were not my target tonight! This is what I am here for! And the mandatory Sai Krok Issan (Issan Sausage) Yea… I don’t care if they are state champions, I am still not trying these bugs! If you haven’t tried TFC (Thai Fried Chicken), do yourself a favour and just do it! Edible and non-edible plants. Live music and chill zone.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      }
